# Domain layer

- Do not import from `src/infra`.
- Expected failures return `Either` (`left` / `right`), not thrown exceptions.
- One use case = one application action (`CreateRecipe`, `PublishRecipe`, …).
- Keep repository ports small; Prisma and in-memory adapters must honor the same contract.
- **`actorId`** is the authenticated chef (`user.sub`); **`authorId`** is the recipe owner. If they differ on a mutating action → `NotAllowedError`.
- `@Injectable()` on use cases only — intentional (MF-07); see `AGENTS.md`. Unit tests use `new UseCase(...)` with in-memory repos, no Nest container.
